WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.570 --> 00:00:05.880
Dances, dragons, and a whole lot of death
—this is the life of Rhaenyra Targaryen.

00:00:05.880 --> 00:00:09.499
Beware: heavy spoilers for "House of the Dragon"
lie ahead.

00:00:09.772 --> 00:00:16.890
Born in 97 AC, Princess Rhaenyra is the firstborn
child of King Viserys I and Queen Aemma.

00:00:16.890 --> 00:00:20.230
Rhaenyra's father inherits the throne in a
time of turmoil.

00:00:20.230 --> 00:00:25.160
The fifth king of the Targaryen dynasty is
chosen to rule by the Great Council of 101

00:00:25.160 --> 00:00:30.330
AC after the old king, Jaehaerys I, loses
both of his male heirs.

00:00:30.330 --> 00:00:35.470
Jaeherys convenes the noble houses of Westeros
to decide who will inherit the crown as his successor.

00:00:35.470 --> 00:00:40.410
Viserys is chosen over his cousin Rhaenys,
despite being the younger of the two.

00:00:40.410 --> 00:00:45.149
Rhaenys, nicknamed the Queen Who Never Was,
discusses the Great Council's decision with

00:00:45.149 --> 00:00:49.210
young Rhaenyra in the second episode of House
of the Dragon, telling the princess:

00:00:49.210 --> 00:00:55.587
"Men would sooner put the realm to the torch
than see a woman ascend the Iron Throne."

00:00:55.587 --> 00:01:00.520
Viserys and Aemma try multiple times to conceive
a male heir throughout their marriage, resulting

00:01:00.520 --> 00:01:06.757
in several miscarriages, stillbirths, and,
ultimately, a brutal and bloody fate for Queen Aemma.

00:01:06.757 --> 00:01:11.810
After a non-consensual medieval C-section
ends the queen's life, the teenage Rhaenyra

00:01:11.810 --> 00:01:14.240
is officially named Viserys' heir.

00:01:14.240 --> 00:01:18.610
This differs slightly from Fire And Blood
— in the book, Viserys names Rhaenyra his

00:01:18.610 --> 00:01:21.102
heir when she is just eight years old.

00:01:21.249 --> 00:01:26.280
King Viserys I defies tradition in naming
his daughter the heir to the Iron Throne.

00:01:26.280 --> 00:01:30.630
However, the king does a half-hearted job
of securing Rhaenyra's position of power,

00:01:30.630 --> 00:01:33.790
especially after he has sons by Alicent Hightower.

00:01:33.790 --> 00:01:38.400
Rather than challenge male primogeniture,
or make a formal declaration of Targaryen

00:01:38.400 --> 00:01:43.690
exceptionalism, Viserys seemingly just hopes
for the best, oblivious to the civil war flaring

00:01:43.690 --> 00:01:44.700
up around him.

00:01:44.700 --> 00:01:49.180
House of the Dragon suggests that Viserys
is motivated by a mixture of guilt for Aemma's

00:01:49.180 --> 00:01:53.380
death and a desire to keep his hot-headed
brother Daemon away from the throne.

00:01:53.380 --> 00:01:55.159
Does Viserys love his daughter?

00:01:55.159 --> 00:01:55.791
Yes.

00:01:55.791 --> 00:01:59.266
But doesn't that mean he should work harder
to secure her future as queen?

00:01:59.266 --> 00:02:00.499
Probably.

00:02:00.848 --> 00:02:05.580
Rhaenyra is beloved by the people of Westeros during her youth, so much so that they dub 

00:02:05.580 --> 00:02:08.390
her "The Realm's Delight" in honor of her
esteemed beauty.

00:02:08.390 --> 00:02:13.300
As a child, she serves as a cupbearer to her
father, which gives her access to all of his

00:02:13.300 --> 00:02:17.780
council meetings and first-hand experience
of the inner machinations of governance.

00:02:17.780 --> 00:02:21.800
Rhaenyra's reputation plummets over the course
of her life, however.

00:02:21.800 --> 00:02:25.910
Fire and Blood tells us the Targaryen queen
became a controversial figure in her later

00:02:25.910 --> 00:02:30.520
years, earning some very unsavory nicknames
from the people of Westeros.

00:02:30.520 --> 00:02:35.340
Young Rhaenyra is portrayed by Milly Alcock
in House of the Dragon, while actor Emma D'Arcy

00:02:35.340 --> 00:02:39.000
later takes over the role as an older version
of the character.

00:02:39.000 --> 00:02:44.390
Casting two actors to portray Rhaenyra might
be more than a practical decision on the showrunners' behalf.

00:02:44.390 --> 00:02:49.100
By seeing two versions of Rhaenyra, viewers
get to experience the distinct phases of Rhaenyra's

00:02:49.100 --> 00:02:54.170
life, and see how her experience in Westerosi
politics changes her over time.

00:02:54.170 --> 00:02:58.450
In one of the earliest scenes in House of
the Dragon, Rhaenyra soars over King's Landing

00:02:58.450 --> 00:03:00.060
on the back of her dragon.

00:03:00.060 --> 00:03:05.550
Rhaenyra rides the dragon Syrax, nicknamed
the "Golden Beast" for her striking gold scales.

00:03:05.550 --> 00:03:10.620
Named after a Valyrian goddess, Syrax is less
aggressive and battle-worn than Prince Daemon's

00:03:10.620 --> 00:03:12.670
dragon, Caraxes the Blood Wyrm.

00:03:12.670 --> 00:03:15.740
Nevertheless, Syrax is a force to be reckoned
with.

00:03:15.740 --> 00:03:22.297
"They're a power man should never have trifled
with — one that brought Valyria its doom."

00:03:22.530 --> 00:03:26.920
Rhaenyra takes to the sky on Syrax for the
first time at the tender age of seven.

00:03:26.920 --> 00:03:32.310
Unlike other famous Targaryen dragons, such
as Balerion the Black Dread, Syrax only has

00:03:32.310 --> 00:03:34.170
one rider throughout her life.

00:03:34.170 --> 00:03:38.760
In Fire and Blood, Rhaenyra's son, Prince
Joffrey, attempts to fly Syrax — only for

00:03:38.760 --> 00:03:42.660
the dragon to reject her rider and throw him
from her back to his death.

00:03:42.660 --> 00:03:47.004
It's clear from the opening of House of the
Dragon that Rhaenyra and Syrax have a close bond.

00:03:47.004 --> 00:03:50.890
But this is Westeros, where happy endings
are few and far between.

00:03:50.890 --> 00:03:55.560
Fire and Blood hands down a terrible fate
for Syrax, who is killed by a rioting mob

00:03:55.560 --> 00:03:59.039
that storms the Dragonpit in defiance of the
Targaryens.

00:03:59.039 --> 00:04:04.040
In the long and bloody history of Westeros,
Rhaenyra Targaryen is the first woman to sit

00:04:04.040 --> 00:04:05.420
on the Iron Throne.

00:04:05.420 --> 00:04:11.190
She later has her reign disputed and discredited
by her rival Aegon II, as well as the Maesters

00:04:11.190 --> 00:04:14.190
of the Citadel, who denounce her as a usurper.

00:04:14.190 --> 00:04:18.950
However, Rhaenyra nevertheless sits on the
throne after her faction, known as the Blacks,

00:04:18.950 --> 00:04:20.670
takes King's Landing from Aegon.

00:04:20.670 --> 00:04:25.680
Rhaenyra rules for six months in King's Landing,
earning her the moniker "The Half-Year Queen."

00:04:25.680 --> 00:04:29.970
Book lore frames her as the only woman to
have ever sat on the throne, although in Game

00:04:29.970 --> 00:04:35.060
of Thrones, Cersei Lannister follows in Rhaenyra's
footsteps and becomes the Queen of Westeros

00:04:35.060 --> 00:04:38.960
after the deaths of her children in the Season
6 finale.

00:04:38.960 --> 00:04:43.390
Despite her discredited sovereignty, Rhaenyra
remains a powerful figure in the Targaryen

00:04:43.390 --> 00:04:47.390
dynasty and an influential ancestor for Daenerys
in the books.

00:04:47.390 --> 00:04:51.910
The Mother of Dragons is the second sovereign
queen in her family after Rhaenyra, as she

00:04:51.910 --> 00:04:56.719
rules the city of Meereen while laying her
claim to the Iron Throne of Westeros.

00:04:56.719 --> 00:05:01.230
The similarities between Rhaenyra and Cersei
Lannister don't end there, however.

00:05:01.230 --> 00:05:05.750
The Targaryen queen has five children who
are key figures in the Dance of the Dragons.

00:05:05.750 --> 00:05:10.990
Her first three children, Jacaerys, Lucerys,
and Joffrey, are born from Rhaenyra's marriage

00:05:10.990 --> 00:05:12.750
to Ser Laenor Velaryon.

00:05:12.750 --> 00:05:17.590
Like Cersei, however, the legitimacy of her
children is doubted, with the realm speculating

00:05:17.590 --> 00:05:22.600
that the boys are actually the sons of Rhaenyra's
lover, Ser Harwin Strong.

00:05:22.600 --> 00:05:26.049
"We know, father.

00:05:26.049 --> 00:05:29.799
Everyone knows.

00:05:29.799 --> 00:05:31.099
Just look at them."

00:05:31.370 --> 00:05:37.426
Rhaenyra later gives birth to two more sons,
Aegon and Viserys, fathered by Prince Daemon Targaryen.

00:05:37.426 --> 00:05:42.210
Rhaenyra is pregnant with her sixth child
when her father, Viserys, finally dies.

00:05:42.210 --> 00:05:46.931
The news triggers a difficult labor, and tragedy
strikes twice for the Targaryen queen, as

00:05:46.931 --> 00:05:50.000
her daughter, Visenya, does not survive the
birth.

00:05:50.244 --> 00:05:53.920
The first time Rhaenyra Targaryen marries,
it is for duty.

00:05:53.920 --> 00:06:00.398
The princess is wed to Ser Laenor Velaryon
in 114 AC, but makes no secret of her distaste for him.

00:06:00.398 --> 00:06:05.260
Fire and Blood speculates that Rhaenyra was
forced to marry Laenor by Viserys, who threatened

00:06:05.260 --> 00:06:08.560
to denounce her as his heir if she didn't
go through with the marriage.

00:06:08.560 --> 00:06:13.110
It is heavily suggested that Laenor is gay
and in love with Ser Joffrey Lonmouth, with

00:06:13.110 --> 00:06:15.810
whom he spends most of his time at High Tide.

00:06:15.810 --> 00:06:19.930
Despite spending most of her time at court
away from her husband, Rhaenyra becomes friends

00:06:19.930 --> 00:06:25.330
with Laenor's sister, Laena Velaryon, who
marries Daemon Targaryen and, in the book,

00:06:25.330 --> 00:06:27.220
dies giving birth to their twin daughters.

00:06:27.220 --> 00:06:33.760
When Laenor and Laena die in 120 AC, Rhaenyra
and Daemon marry in secret, against the wishes

00:06:33.760 --> 00:06:35.260
of King Viserys.

00:06:35.260 --> 00:06:40.060
Their relationship is creepy right from the
start: Daemon gifts his niece various trinkets

00:06:40.060 --> 00:06:43.071
from his voyages and courts her from a young
age.

00:06:43.071 --> 00:06:48.490
Rhaenyra's formal title as heir to King Viserys
is Princess of Dragonstone, a title passed

00:06:48.490 --> 00:06:50.550
down to all Targaryen heirs.

00:06:50.550 --> 00:06:54.580
Like her ancestor, Daenerys bears this title
at the beginning of Game of Thrones.

00:06:54.580 --> 00:07:00.490
Daenerys serves as heir to her brother Viserys
as the only known Targaryen left after Robert's Rebellion.

00:07:00.490 --> 00:07:05.000
After the deaths of Viserys and her unborn
son Rhaego, Daenerys assumes sovereignty of

00:07:05.000 --> 00:07:08.630
House Targaryen, believing herself to be the
last of the dragonlords.

00:07:08.630 --> 00:07:12.530
Both Daenerys' and Rhaenyra's story arcs are
driven by prophecy.

00:07:12.530 --> 00:07:16.640
In House of the Dragon, Viserys tells his
daughter about a prophetic dream that Aegon

00:07:16.640 --> 00:07:22.530
I once had, a dream that motivated the conqueror
to unify Westeros with fire and blood.

00:07:22.530 --> 00:07:28.450
"Aegon saw absolute darkness riding on those
winds, and whatever dwells within will destroy

00:07:28.450 --> 00:07:30.510
the world of the living."

00:07:30.510 --> 00:07:35.310
The Princess of Dragonstone is heir to her
father's crown and her family's responsibility.

00:07:35.310 --> 00:07:39.730
In order to maintain that responsibility,
Rhaenyra spends a great deal of time fending

00:07:39.730 --> 00:07:45.370
off crown-hungry suitors from other noble
families such as House Lannister, House Frey,

00:07:45.370 --> 00:07:46.770
and House Tyrell.

00:07:47.053 --> 00:07:51.520
King Viserys makes Alicent Hightower his wife
in 106 AC.

00:07:51.520 --> 00:07:56.680
The daughter of Viserys' Hand, Ser Otto Hightower,
Alicent gives birth to four children over

00:07:56.680 --> 00:07:58.010
the next few years.

00:07:58.010 --> 00:08:00.680
The coming of these children makes the realm
anxious.

00:08:00.680 --> 00:08:02.790
Will Rhaenyra remain Viserys' heir?

00:08:02.790 --> 00:08:07.660
Or will patriarchal traditions force the king
to name Prince Aegon, his eldest son, the

00:08:07.660 --> 00:08:09.110
new heir to the throne?

00:08:09.110 --> 00:08:14.550
To the king's credit, Viserys does not budge
— Rhaenyra is the heir, through and through.

00:08:14.550 --> 00:08:18.190
But that doesn't stop the Targaryens from
splintering into two factions.

00:08:18.190 --> 00:08:23.490
In Fire and Blood, Rhaenyra makes a bold statement
by dressing in the traditional Targaryen colors

00:08:23.490 --> 00:08:29.050
to symbolize her status as the future of House
Targaryen, juxtaposing Alicent's green gown.

00:08:29.050 --> 00:08:33.419
The two factions are thereafter dubbed the
blacks and the greens after the princess and

00:08:33.419 --> 00:08:35.240
the queen's costumes.

00:08:35.240 --> 00:08:39.470
Alicent and Aegon lead the greens, with Rhaenyra
and Daemon at the head of their opposition.

00:08:39.470 --> 00:08:44.540
Aegon, who will become known as Aegon II,
rides the dragon Sunfyre, while his brother

00:08:44.540 --> 00:08:49.170
Aemond One-Eye rides Vhagar, the oldest and
largest Targaryen dragon.

00:08:49.170 --> 00:08:52.370
Rhaenyra and Aegon never fight directly on
their dragons.

00:08:52.370 --> 00:08:54.990
Other characters fight — and die — on
their behalf.

00:08:54.990 --> 00:09:00.050
The civil war decimates House Targaryen, wiping
out nearly all of the dragons and triggering

00:09:00.050 --> 00:09:03.190
the steady decline that leads to Robert's
Rebellion.

00:09:03.190 --> 00:09:08.554
Although she rules King's Landing for only
six months, Rhaenyra quickly becomes an unpopular queen.

00:09:08.554 --> 00:09:12.122
The people initially cheer for her when she
takes the throne from her brother, but when

00:09:12.122 --> 00:09:17.150
Rhaenyra hikes taxes dramatically to fund
the war, it is the people of King's Landing

00:09:17.150 --> 00:09:18.820
who pay the price.

00:09:18.820 --> 00:09:21.890
Starving and oppressed, the people rebel against
her.

00:09:21.890 --> 00:09:26.671
Led by a High Sparrow-like figure named the
Shepherd, rioters take over the city, storm

00:09:26.671 --> 00:09:29.620
the Dragonpit and kill a number of dragons.

00:09:29.620 --> 00:09:34.320
Rhaenyra flees to Dragonstone, but Aegon and
his forces wait there in ambush.

00:09:34.320 --> 00:09:38.390
Aegon has had a tough time by this point,
having been severely wounded multiple times

00:09:38.390 --> 00:09:39.730
during the war.

00:09:39.730 --> 00:09:43.420
After capturing Rhaenyra, he sentences her
to death by dragon.

00:09:43.420 --> 00:09:47.180
Sunfyre burns and devours her, all while her
son looks on.

00:09:47.180 --> 00:09:49.770
"It ate her while her son watched.

00:09:49.770 --> 00:09:54.338
What's left of her is buried in the crypts,
right down there."

00:09:54.338 --> 00:09:58.800
Most of what we know about Rhaenyra and her
family comes from Mushroom, a dwarf who served

00:09:58.800 --> 00:10:01.480
as a court jester to the Targaryens.

00:10:01.480 --> 00:10:03.690
Mushroom is a Tyrion Lannister archetype.

00:10:03.690 --> 00:10:07.230
Both share a propensity for wine and bawdy
jokes, for example.

00:10:07.230 --> 00:10:11.570
Most importantly, Mushroom and Tyrion are
underestimated by the people around them.

00:10:11.570 --> 00:10:16.940
Like Tyrion, Mushroom uses this to his advantage
by becoming privy to important information

00:10:16.940 --> 00:10:20.200
that the nobles don't bother to conceal from
him.

00:10:20.200 --> 00:10:25.330
Mushroom documented an account of the Dance
of the Dragons titled The Testimony of Mushroom.

00:10:25.330 --> 00:10:30.360
His testimony forms the backbone of Fire and
Blood, and the narrator of the history book,

00:10:30.360 --> 00:10:34.500
Archmaester Gyldayn, does his best to discern
the truth from the lies.

00:10:34.500 --> 00:10:37.620
Mushroom makes some pretty salacious claims
in his testimony, too.

00:10:37.620 --> 00:10:42.311
Gyldayn compares his account of the events
to other historians, like Septon Eustace and

00:10:42.311 --> 00:10:45.550
Grand Maester Munkun, whose tales often contradict.

00:10:45.550 --> 00:10:49.400
Then again, in Westeros, any scandal is possible.

00:10:49.400 --> 00:10:53.950
Mushroom doesn't appear in House of the Dragon,
though co-creator Ryan Condal has confirmed

00:10:53.950 --> 00:10:56.621
that there will at least be some nods to the
character.

00:10:56.621 --> 00:11:00.860
After Rhaenyra's death, it seems as if Aegon
II has won the war.

00:11:00.860 --> 00:11:02.850
But all is not lost for the queen's cause.

00:11:02.850 --> 00:11:06.900
The blacks continue to fight in her name,
with a new army of Northmen and knights from

00:11:06.900 --> 00:11:09.170
the Vale approaching King's Landing.

00:11:09.170 --> 00:11:14.382
Cregan Stark leads his soldiers to the capital,
where they discover that Aegon II has been poisoned.

00:11:14.382 --> 00:11:18.840
The greens bend the knee to Cregan, who makes
some severe changes in the city on behalf

00:11:18.840 --> 00:11:22.050
of Rhaenyra's son, the future King Aegon III.

00:11:22.050 --> 00:11:25.029
Cregan's six-day rule is dubbed the "Hour
of the Wolf."

00:11:25.029 --> 00:11:27.400
With it, the Dance of the Dragons comes to
an end.

00:11:27.400 --> 00:11:32.180
Aegon III is crowned at the age of eleven,
though the young king remains deeply traumatized

00:11:32.180 --> 00:11:35.830
by the death of his mother and falls into
a life-long depression.

00:11:35.830 --> 00:11:40.210
It is during Aegon's reign that the last of
the Targaryen dragons dies, earning him the

00:11:40.210 --> 00:11:41.940
nickname Dragonbane.

00:11:41.940 --> 00:11:46.040
And while Rhaenyra might not win the throne
in the end, her legacy lives on — as her

00:11:46.040 --> 00:11:52.199
ancestry extends all the way to Jon Snow and
Daenerys Targaryen, the last scions of the House of the Dragon.

